n: 4.5.8
name: keep
kind: hub
is: Eight proposals kept from the reading's 22: acknowledgment as evaluation rule, three primitives, transactional effects, determinism on the blueprint, (data, witness) references, flattening and one generics mechanism, identity at freeze, capability references.
at: 2026-11-24

n: 4.5.8.1
name: ack-is-the-evaluation-rule
kind: finding
is: Proposal: every expression yields nothing, 0, 1 or node(s) as its evaluation rule, with no booleans for control. 0, an answered no, triggers backtracking; nothing, no answer, triggers hold or timeout handling and is never read as a verdict. A timeout is the clock acknowledging nothing to a delimiter.
status: inferred
conf: low
from: 1.1 1.5 1.7.17 1.7.19 4.5.1.2 4.5.1.3 4.5.3.8
limit: The node's own premise 1.7.17 reads fail as nothing: core-axioms.form lines 170-172 say 'The core had read the nothing-ground twice, and both readings were terminal: FAIL ("it did not land") and STOP'
at: 2026-11-24

n: 4.5.8.2
name: three-control-primitives
kind: finding
is: Proposal: the surface has fail, ordered choice and one choice-consuming delimiter of split shape, with one and all as its common forms; if, not, every, try and cut are sugar. Operations with handlers are the general control form, in three declared resume classes: never resumes, resumes once in tail position, may resume later or more than once.
status: inferred
conf: mid
from: 4.5.1.3 4.5.1.4 4.5.1.7 4.5.1.10
limit: Default strength and the scope of cut are listed as not ready.
at: 2026-11-24

n: 4.5.8.3
name: transactional-effects-on-a-choice-stack
kind: finding
is: Proposal: every effect inside a choice-consuming delimiter is transactional. Immutable content-addressed nodes need no undo, since restore is repointing; live mutable cells get a value trail scoped to the innermost choice point; effects that left the body are forbidden there or declare a compensating recipe. Suspension is one-shot stack switching.
status: inferred
conf: mid
from: 4.5.1.1 4.5.1.4 4.5.1.8 4.5.1.9 1.3 1.7.8
limit: Not run; the costs behind the choice of a choice-point stack with a value trail are counts from published layouts.
at: 2026-11-24

n: 4.5.8.4
name: determinism-on-the-blueprint
kind: finding
is: Proposal: infer a determinism per recipe on Mercury's lattice and store it on the blueprint. A det recipe compiles with no choice machinery, a semidet one as a conditional branch, and only nondet recipes touch the choice stack. Tabling keyed by recipe id and argument ids follows from content addressing and covers packrat parsing.
status: inferred
conf: mid
from: 4.5.1.6 4.5.1.1 1.3
limit: That packrat parsing buys linear time by memoising every (rule, position) result is from model memory; no compile was run.
at: 2026-11-24

n: 4.5.8.5
name: data-witness-references
kind: finding
is: Proposal: a reference is a (data, witness) pair and data never contains a table pointer, so the data's bytes and content address are the same through every interface. Witnesses are computed on demand and memoised by (shape id, interface id); with content addresses that cache never goes invalid. Conformance is structural and can be added later.
status: inferred
conf: mid
from: 4.5.2.1 4.5.2.2 4.5.2.3 4.5.2.7 1.3 1.4
see: 3.12.4.1 3.12.2.1 3.12.2.2
limit: The cost figures are counts, not measurements.
at: 2026-11-24

n: 4.5.8.6
name: flattening-and-one-generics-mechanism
kind: finding
is: Proposal: several parents compose by flattening into a new shape with conflicts resolved in the text, with no subobjects and no pointer adjustment. Templates and generics are one mechanism: recipes that take blueprints as arguments, run by passing a dictionary or specialised into machine code cached by (recipe id, argument shape ids).
status: inferred
conf: low
from: 4.5.2.4 4.5.2.5 4.5.2.6 4.5.2.7
see: 3.12.2.4 3.12.4.4 3.12.4.5 3.12.4.8
limit: Flattening of a second class base is what the 2026 body does (3.12.2.4); its fixture stood under a pinned Verdict 119 at commit 1044906a5 of 2026-09-15 and was deleted by the cut of 2026-09-29 (3.12.4.4, 3.12.4.5). Delegation to separate base objects has no record of running in either era (3.12.4.8)
at: 2026-11-24

n: 4.5.8.7
name: identity-at-freeze-counted-references
kind: finding
is: Proposal: identity is computed only when a node freezes, as a hash of its canonical numeric form (kind number, child ids, literal bytes), names kept apart. Frozen nodes are immutable and reclaimed by precise reference counting with reuse; a Merkle DAG has no cycles, so counting finds everything unreferenced. Live nodes are addressed by location.
status: inferred
conf: mid
src: 2.1.4#575 2.1.4#585
from: 4.5.3.1 4.5.3.2 4.5.3.3 4.5.3.4 1.3 1.7.2
see: 3.14 3.15.2.2
limit: The reading mapped frozen, live and transient onto ice, water and gas from two lines of the old body's AGENTS.md and marked the mapping assumed; hub 3.14 has since traced the three words to 2025-09-09 and counted 21 uses on 12 axes. The reading measured no hash; hub 3.15 has since measured direct SHA-256 at 16.0 ns per 40-byte digest on one Apple M4 Max, with synthetic nodes (3.15.2.2)
at: 2026-11-24

n: 4.5.8.8
name: capability-references-one-offer
kind: finding
is: Proposal: a reference crossing a cell boundary is a capability in three modes: frozen (shared freely), unique live (moved) or opaque handle (compared and offered to, never read). A crossing outside an offered witness fails a check and leaves a record. Offer is one primitive: a direct call when det and local, else enqueue plus future.
status: inferred
conf: mid
from: 4.5.3.5 4.5.3.6 4.5.3.7 4.5.3.8 1.4 1.5
limit: Promise pipelining and eventual sends were recalled from model memory, not read.
at: 2026-11-24

n: 4.5.9
name: drop
kind: hub
is: Five things the reading argues against: multi-shot continuations as the base of choice; a table pointer inside the object; booleans and exception-typed timeouts as carriers of control; hashing every intermediate value at run time; ambient authority and per-cell event loops. The reading has no let-go list; these come from its proposals and cautions.
at: 2026-11-24

n: 4.5.9.1
name: multi-shot-continuations-as-choice-substrate
kind: finding
is: Drop multi-shot continuations as the base of choice. Chronological backtracking does not need them: the WAM re-enters each alternative from saved registers and copies no stack, and OCaml 5 and WebAssembly stack switching are one-shot by design. Multi-shot is paid only where a resumption escapes as a value and is frozen into a node.
status: inferred
conf: mid
from: 4.5.1.1 4.5.1.8
limit: Inferred from published frame layouts and manuals; no timing compares a choice-point stack with cloned continuations on the target machine.
at: 2026-11-24

n: 4.5.9.2
name: table-pointer-inside-the-object
kind: finding
is: Drop the table pointer inside the object and base subobjects. The offsets, thunks, secondary tables and table of tables of the Itanium C++ ABI exist because the table pointer lives in the object and each base needs its own view of 'this'; an embedded pointer would also put an address inside content that is hashed for identity.
status: inferred
conf: mid
from: 4.5.2.3 4.5.2.1 1.3
limit: Inferred from the ABI text and the Go layout. It covers interface inheritance; shared base state, which delegation provides, is the open half named in the keep hub.
at: 2026-11-24

n: 4.5.9.4
name: hashing-every-intermediate-value
kind: finding
is: Drop hashing of every intermediate value at run time: a 40-byte node costs 1.2 to 2.3 ns without identity against 28.1 to 44.8 ns minted with one into a store of 16.8 million nodes. Identity is computed when a node freezes and not while it is being worked on.
status: inferred
conf: low
from: 4.5.3.1 4.5.3.2 3.15.4.1
limit: 4.5.3.1 and 4.5.3.2 say nothing about run-time cost. That hash consing pays off only for immutable, frequently compared structure is the reading's own inference; its encyclopedia source, not encoded here, says only that equality becomes a pointer comparison, usually with a hash table of weak references (line 242).
at: 2026-11-24

